-- title:
--   Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of the away-from-r̄ r Hecke tower
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $r$ and $\bar r$ are distinct primes, $N$ is a nonzero squarefree natural number divisible by neither, and the following data are fixed.
--
--   **Base rings.** $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain with uniformiser $\pi$ ($\pi$ irreducible, $\mathcal O$ complete for the $(\pi)$-adic topology), whose residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements and which satisfies $(r)=(\pi)$; $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$. $\mathrm{Onr}$ is a characteristic-zero $\mathcal O$-domain, complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$, with that ideal maximal, such that every element of $\mathrm{Onr}$ satisfies a monic $\mathcal O$-polynomial modulo $\pi$ and every monic polynomial of positive degree over $\mathrm{Onr}$ has a root modulo $\pi$ (so $\mathrm{Onr}/(\pi)$ is an algebraic closure of $\mathcal O/(\pi)$); $\mathrm{Fr}$ is an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism of $\mathrm{Onr}$ with $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod{\pi}$. Finally $\mathrm{vdet}:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) is the homomorphism characterised by $\mathrm{vdet}(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g=u\,\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Indefinite side and moduli.** $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ is indefinite and ramified exactly at $r$ and $\bar r$ (the predicate `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`: $0<a$ or $0<b$, and for a finite place $v$ the completed algebra is a division algebra precisely when $v$ lies above $r$ or above $\bar r$), and $\Lambda$ is a maximal order in it containing all rational integers (hypothesis `hΛℤ`). The scheme $\mathcal X$ with structure morphism $f$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, together with the point assignment `pt`, is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves with $\Gamma_0(N)$-level structure over $\mathcal O$-schemes (`IsCoarseModuli`: invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change, bijectivity on geometric points, and the universal property). An auxiliary level $n\ge 3$ is prime to $r$, to $\bar r$ and to $N$; $M$ with $f_M$ and `ptF` is a *fine* moduli space for such curves equipped with a full level-$n$ point (`IsFineModuli`), $G$ acts on $M$ through $\rho:G\to\operatorname{Aut}M$ with labels $\chi:G\to\Lambda$ as a level-twist action (`IsLevelTwistAction`), and $p:M\to\mathcal X$ is the forgetful morphism over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, invariant under $\rho$ and compatible with the two point assignments. For every prime $\ell$ distinct from $r$ and $\bar r$ (the type `HeckeTower.AwayPrime r rbar`), $\mathcal Y_\ell$ with $g_\ell$ and $\mathrm{ptT}_\ell$ is a coarse moduli space for curves with an extra level-$\ell$ subgroup scheme (`IsCoarseModuliT`), and $d_0^\ell,d_1^\ell:\mathcal Y_\ell\to\mathcal X$ are the two degeneracy morphisms over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, $d_0^\ell$ forgetting the subgroup and $d_1^\ell$ recording the quotient by it (hypotheses `hd₀`, `hd₁`). Endomorphisms $a_r,a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ realise the Atkin–Lehner involutions at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points.
--
--   **Definite side.** $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ is definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$, $\Lambda_1$ is a maximal order, $R_1\le\Lambda_1$ is an Eichler order of level $N$, and $n_1$ lies in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ with $\mathrm{meetOrder}(R_1,n_1)$ an Eichler order of level $Nr$; $\iota_0$ is an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\to M_2(K_0)$, and $v$ is the finite place above $r$. The group $\Gamma_t$ consists of the units lying in the local box units of $R_1$ away from $v$. For each $\ell$ away from $r,\bar r$ there are a unit $s_\ell$ and an adelic unit $sf_\ell$ such that (hypothesis `hs`) $sf_\ell$ has component $s_\ell\otimes 1$ at every place not above $r$ and component $1$ at places above $r$, the product of the diagonal image of the scalar $\ell$ with $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in $\mathrm{levelHeckeUSet}(\Lambda_1,\mathrm{meetOrder}(R_1,n_1),\ell)$ when $\ell\mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of $\mathrm{meetOrder}(R_1,n_1)$ at $\ell$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$; and $\Gamma_{t,\ell}=\Gamma_t\cap s_\ell\Gamma_t s_\ell^{-1}$. A unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalises $\Gamma_t$.
--
--   **Data in characteristic $r$.** $\mathrm{coord}$ is an order coordinate for $\Lambda$ at $r$ (`IsOrderCoord`: additive, unital, multiplicative in the twisted sense, injective, $r$-adically dense, and matching traces). Over the residue ring $\mathrm{Onr}/(\pi)$ there are a fake elliptic curve $A_0$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$, formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of $A_0$ of dimension $2$ realising $A_0$ as a formal module via $\mathrm{coord}$ and $X_0$, and families $e,e'$ of endomorphisms of $A_0$ indexed by $\Gamma_t$ together with degrees $\deg$. The hypotheses `hE1`, `hE1mul`, `hE1sc`, `hE1'`, `hE2`, `hE3`, `hE4` (the endomorphism dictionary for $\Gamma_t$, summarised here) state: each $(e\gamma,e'\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the $\Gamma_0(N)$-level; $e$ is multiplicative up to $r$-power multiplication; rational scalars in $\Gamma_t$ act by the corresponding integer up to $r$-powers, and conversely only scalars act by integers; for every injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and $X_0$-uniformiser into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ with, for each $\gamma$, a centraliser element $\varepsilon$ and $k_\gamma\in\mathbb Z$ whose induced substitution on $\theta_0$ at nilpotent arguments realises $e\gamma$ and with $E_0\varepsilon=r^{k_\gamma}\,g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$; each full level-$n$ point of $A_0$ is moved by $e\gamma$ through the action of a label $\mathrm{lab}(\gamma)\in\Lambda$, multiplicative and scalar-compatible modulo $n$; and every level-preserving $r$-power isogeny endomorphism of a fake elliptic curve over an algebraically closed field pulled back from $A_0$ comes from some $e\gamma$ up to $r$-powers.
--
--   The orders $R_2\le R_1$ and $R_2'\le\Lambda_{1s}$ (with $\Lambda_{1s}$ a second maximal order such that $\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_{1s}=R_1$, and $R_2\le R_2'$), both $r$-saturated in the sense that every element of $R_1$, respectively of $\Lambda_{1s}$, becomes an element of $R_2$, respectively $R_2'$, after multiplication by a power of $r$, carry families $\hat e$ and $\hat e'$ of endomorphisms of $A_0$. The hypotheses `hE5a`–`hE5g` and `hE6a`–`hE6f` (summarised here) require that $\hat e$ and $\hat e'$ are additive for the relative group law, commute with the $\Lambda$-action, preserve the level in the case of $\hat e$, send $1$ to the identity, are multiplicative in the contravariant sense, send a rational integer to the corresponding $\Lambda$-action, satisfy $\hat e(\bar x)\circ\hat e(x)$ (in diagrammatic order $\hat e\,\bar x$ followed by $\hat e\,x$) $=$ the action of $\mathrm{nrd}(x)$, agree with $e$ on $r$-power multiples of elements of $\Gamma_t$, admit a joint matrix dictionary as in `hE2` for both $\Gamma_t$ and $R_2$, and are stable under the main involution; in addition $\hat e'$ extends $\hat e$, is injective, and for a prime $q\ne r$ an element $z$ of $R_2'$ killing the $q$-torsion satisfies $r^{K}z=q\,y$ for some $y\in\Lambda_{1s}$ and some $K$.
--
--   **Drinfeld side.** $\iota:\mathbb Z_{r^2}\to\mathrm{Onr}$ is a ring map; $\Phi$ is a special formal $\mathcal O$-module of height $4$ over $\mathrm{Onr}/(r)$; $MD$ is a moduli package for $r$ over $\mathrm{Onr}$ satisfying the Zariski sheaf condition; $\eta$ assigns to each rigidified object over a ring $B$ with $r$ nilpotent a point of $MD$, and `hη` states (three clauses) that on Noetherian $B$ it identifies admissible rigidified objects up to isomorphism, is natural in $B$, and is locally surjective over a distinguished open cover. $E_0$ is an injective ring map from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and $\Phi$-uniformiser into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is, up to a fixed power of $r$, the matrices with entries in $\mathcal O$ (hypothesis `hE₀`). The family $eD$, with `hnatD`, `hbijD`, `hfstD`, `hGLD`, `hPiD`, `hPiexD`, identifies naturally and bijectively, on Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, the functor of $MD$-points with $B\mapsto(\mathrm{Onr}\to_{\mathcal O}B)\times\hat\Omega(B)$, compatibly with the structure map to $\mathrm{Onr}$, carrying the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action `ModuliPackage.G.IsActBy` to the twisted action `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` (in which the $\mathrm{Onr}$-component is twisted by $\mathrm{Fr}^{-\mathrm{vdet}}$ and the Deligne datum is pulled back along $g^{-1}$), carrying $\pi$-translation to the Frobenius twist of the first coordinate, and with $\pi$-translates always existing.
--
--   Further, $\kappa$ reduces $\mathrm{Onr}/(\pi)$ to $\mathrm{Onr}/(r)$ compatibly with the quotient maps, and $\beta_0$ is an isogeny of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the base change of $X_0$ along $\kappa$; $P_0$ is a full level-$n$ point of $A_0$; $A_{0w}$ with $a_w,a_w',b_w,b_w'$ realises the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ of $A_0$ followed by an $r^{k_w}$-isogeny back to $A_0$ preserving the level, and `hJOINTw` supplies the matrix dictionary for $\Gamma_t$ together with a centraliser element realising the composite $a_w$ followed by $b_w$ and matching $r^{k_w}g\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g^{-1}$.
--
--   **Transfer to the Drinfeld moduli problem.** $\Xi$ sends a rigidified curve over a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent to a $G$-point of $MD$; `hΞleg`, `hΞnat`, `hΞiso`, `hΞdef` state that on connected $B$ the structure map of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$, that $\Xi$ is compatible with pullback of rigidified curves, that it is unchanged under isomorphisms of rigidified curves in the stated sense, and that on connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent it is computed, for any formal module structure on the curve, by a rigid transport with $j\le 1$ and the corresponding admissible rigidified object. With $g_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ fixed, `heqΓ`, `heqW`, `heqS` state that translating a rigidification by $e\gamma$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$, by the $\bar r$-Atkin–Lehner composite, and by the $\ell$-level isogeny composite associated with $s_\ell$ (under the hypotheses on $n_1$, $s$, $sf$ restated there) moves $\Xi$ by the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action of $r^{c}\,g_0\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g_0^{-1}$, of $r^{c}\,g_0\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g_0^{-1}$, and of $r^{c}\,g_0\,\iota_0(\ell\,s_\ell^{-1})\,g_0^{-1}$ respectively, for some $c\in\mathbb Z$.
--
--   **The uniformisation of $M$.** $\theta_t:\Gamma_t\to G$ is a group homomorphism and $\Theta_f$ assigns, to an $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and a triple consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\mathrm{Onr}\to B$, a Deligne datum over $B$ and an element of $G$, a $B$-point of $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$. The hypotheses `hnat`, `hG`, `hi'`, `het`, `hfib` state that $\Theta_f$ is natural in $B$, that $\rho(h)$ carries $\Theta_f(x,gh)$ to $\Theta_f(x,g)$, that $\Theta_f(x',\theta_t(\gamma)g)=\Theta_f(x,g)$ whenever $x'$ is the twisted translate of $x$ by $\iota_0(\gamma)$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$, that $\Theta_f$ has the unique-lifting property along surjections whose kernel has zero product, and that over algebraically closed fields two values of $\Theta_f$ coincide exactly when they differ by some $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$ in the prescribed way (equality of $G$-components up to $\theta_t(\gamma)$, pullback of Deligne data along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$, and agreement of the $\mathrm{Onr}$-components after the Frobenius twist by $-\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0(\gamma))$ on those elements fixed by the scalar subgroup in the kernel of $\theta_t$). Finally the hypotheses `hC0e`, `hC0u`, `hC1e`, `hC1u`, `hC1p`, `hC2`, `hC2c`, `hC3`, `hC4`, `hC4pi`, `hC5` (summarised here) describe how curves with rigidification over Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras with $\pi$ nilpotent correspond to points of $(\mathrm{Onr}\to_{\mathcal O}B)\times\hat\Omega(B)$ via $\Xi$ and $eD$ twisted by $g_0^{-1}$: existence and uniqueness of the norm-compatible level-$n$ transport of $P_0$, existence, uniqueness up to isomorphism and pullback-stability of the even rigidified pair attached to a point, the identification of $\Theta_f(\cdot,1)$ with the moduli point of the corresponding curve with its transported level structure and with its image in $\mathcal X$, the effect of a $\Gamma_t$-translation on the level structure (through $\chi\circ\theta_t$) and on extra level-$\ell$ subgroups, the corresponding statement for a general $\mathrm{GL}_2$-translate and for the $\pi$-translate, and, over algebraically closed fields, the recognition of isomorphisms of the underlying curves by elements $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$, with the induced identification of level-$n$ points and the criterion for extra level-$\ell$ subgroups in terms of the stability of a subgroup of $A_0$ under $e\gamma$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists a family $\Theta_T$ assigning to each prime $\ell$ away from $r,\bar r$ and to each Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent a map from $(\mathrm{Onr}\to_{\mathcal O}B)\times\hat\Omega(B)$ to the $B$-points of $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, such that the following six assertions hold.
--
--   1.
--
--   For each $\ell$, $\Theta_T^\ell$ is natural: for $\mathcal O$-algebra maps $\varphi:B\to B'$ between Noetherian algebras with $\pi$ nilpotent, $\Theta_T^\ell$ applied to the image of $x$ equals the image under $\varphi$ of $\Theta_T^\ell(x)$.
--
--   2.
--
--   For each $\ell$, $\Theta_T^\ell$ is invariant under $\Gamma_{t,\ell}$: if $\gamma\in\Gamma_{t,\ell}$ and $x'$ is the twisted translate of $x$ by $\iota_0(\gamma)$ in the sense of `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct`, then $\Theta_T^\ell(x')=\Theta_T^\ell(x)$.
--
--   3.
--
--   For each $\ell$ and each algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent, and each $\psi:\mathrm{Onr}\to_{\mathcal O}k$: two values $\Theta_T^\ell(\psi,P)$ and $\Theta_T^\ell(\psi,P')$ are equal if and only if there is $\gamma\in\Gamma_{t,\ell}$ with $(\psi,P')$ the twisted translate of $(\psi,P)$ by $\iota_0(\gamma)$.
--
--   4.
--
--   For each $\ell$ and each datum consisting of a scheme $M_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point assignment $\mathrm{ptF}_\ell$ making it a fine moduli space for curves with full level $n$ and an extra level-$\ell$ subgroup (`IsFineModuliT`), a morphism $\pi_\ell:M_\ell\to M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ forgetting the extra level on points, a morphism $p_\ell:M_\ell\to\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ inducing $\mathrm{ptT}_\ell$ on points, and an action $\rho_\ell:G\to\operatorname{Aut}M_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with $\rho_\ell(h)$ followed by $\pi_\ell$ equal to $\pi_\ell$ followed by $\rho(h)$, fixing $p_\ell$, and twisting points by $\chi(h)$ in the sense of `FakeEllipticCurve.WithFullLevel.IsTwistVia` together with matching of the extra level subgroups — there exists $\Theta_{f,\ell}$, defined on Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and taking a triple (map $\mathrm{Onr}\to_{\mathcal O}B$, Deligne datum, element of $G$) to a $B$-point of $M_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, such that: $\Theta_{f,\ell}$ is natural in $B$; $\rho_\ell(h)$ carries $\Theta_{f,\ell}(x,gh)$ to $\Theta_{f,\ell}(x,g)$; for $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$ which also lies in $\Gamma_{t,\ell}$ and $x'$ the twisted translate of $x$ by $\iota_0(\gamma)$ one has $\Theta_{f,\ell}(x',\theta_t(\gamma)g)=\Theta_{f,\ell}(x,g)$; $\Theta_{f,\ell}$ has the unique-lifting property along every surjection $B\to B_0$ of Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras with $\pi$ nilpotent whose kernel has zero product, namely any $B$-point of $M_\ell$ lifting a value $\Theta_{f,\ell}(x_0)$ is $\Theta_{f,\ell}(x)$ for a unique $x$ lifting $x_0$; over an algebraically closed field $k$, $\Theta_{f,\ell}((\psi,P),g)=\Theta_{f,\ell}((\psi',P'),g')$ holds if and only if there is $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_{t,\ell}$, $g'=\theta_t(\gamma)g$, $P'$ the pullback of $P$ along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$, and $\psi'$ agreeing with the Frobenius twist of $\psi$ by $-\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0(\gamma))$ on all elements fixed by the relevant powers of $\mathrm{Fr}$ coming from scalar elements of $\Gamma_t$ in the kernel of $\theta_t$; composing $\Theta_{f,\ell}$ with $\pi_\ell$ gives $\Theta_f$; and composing $\Theta_{f,\ell}(\cdot,1)$ with $p_\ell$ gives $\Theta_T^\ell$.
--
--   5.
--
--   For each $\ell$, composing $\Theta_T^\ell(x)$ with $d_0^\ell$ gives the composite of $\Theta_f(x,1)$ with $p$.
--
--   6.
--
--   For each $\ell$, whenever $x$ is the twisted translate of $x'$ by $\iota_0(s_\ell)$ in the sense of `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct`, composing $\Theta_T^\ell(x)$ with $d_1^\ell$ gives the composite of $\Theta_f(x',1)$ with $p$.
--
--   This is the Hecke-tower step of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation for the Shimura curve attached to an indefinite quaternion algebra ramified exactly at $r$ and $\bar r$: the formal uniformisation $\Theta_f$ of the fine moduli scheme with full level $n$ is transported to the coarse moduli schemes $\mathcal Y_\ell$ carrying an extra level-$\ell$ subgroup, with the quotient group at $\ell$ being $\Gamma_t\cap s_\ell\Gamma_t s_\ell^{-1}$, and the two degeneracy morphisms realised by translation by $s_\ell$ on the Drinfeld side. Here the test algebras are restricted to Noetherian ones; the statement is cited by the variant of the same result without that restriction.
